{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1372694-mortal-martial-artists","id":1372694,"title":"Mortal Martial Artists","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-03-04T06:07:58-08:00","id":1372694,"title":"Mortal Martial Artists","content":"Do mortal martial artists play any significant role in your stories? I'm keen to have mortal dojos running around the setting. Say, that brothel is actually run by Dreaming Pearl Courtesan stylists who keep a library of secrets to build political power. This criminal gang is actually a school of corrupt Ebon Shadow Stylists that my ESS player can either defeat or take over and reform. Some wise Crane Stylists keep a tea shop and help people navigate personal crises, Black Claw stylists hang out being creepy and probably worshiping demons, and literally every other dojo is plagued by brash White Reaper Stylists challenging them to prove their worth.<br /> <br /> Different dojos of the same style could be loosely affiliated, but still distinct. Most of them could count on each other for shelter and support (White Reaper Stylists will probably fight each other, but they'll have a beer together afterwards.)<br /> <br /> The trouble I have is that there isn't a lot of mechanical difference between them. I can sort of dummy it up a bit by giving them relevant specialties (i.e. Ebon Shadow Stylists get a MA specialty in &quot;surprise attacks,&quot; White Reaper Stylists get one in &quot;while outnumbered&quot;) but I doubt player characters would even know the difference. Maybe I could make up some custom merits, or figure out some way to give them very limited access to charms? Do any of you have better ideas?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24421-katamari_naneke","name":"Katamari_Naneke","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"83"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-04T07:04:27-08:00","id":1372703,"title":"","content":"&quot;Do mortal martial artists play any significant role in your stories?&quot;<br /> <br /> 3E? No.<br /> <br /> There is, explicitly, a group of mortal immaculates who have helped out the PCs -- but it's a very minor, background role. Your ideas seem cool though -- maybe next arc?<br /> <br /> &quot;The trouble I have is that there isn't a lot of mechanical difference between them.&quot;<br /> <br /> I think narrating it is the best way forward. Describe attacks using the description of the charms from that style (but don't use the mechanical effects).<br /> <br /> For example, check out the rules on wielding two weapons on page 586. You could totally have a mortal Dreaming Pearl Courtesan stab people in the face with tea cups, whilst mechically modeling it as an unarmed attack. Have the Crane Stylists all flurry Defend Other on each other along with Social Influence to stop the fight. Likewise you can have your Ebon Shadow Stylists drop smoke bombs and try to establish stealth in combat, and stunt their attacks as targetting the weak points in their foe's armor (no mechanical effect). Black Claws who start fights then loudly shout &quot;I didn't start this fight, but I'm going to finish it!&quot; or &quot;Sure I started it, but I'm only trying to protect the one I love!&quot;<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=RmqqNrg2cKg\" target=\"_blank\">NSFW: White Reaper takes on four Earth Dragon Stylists. Is rescued by a Dreaming Pearl Courtesan master.</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-04T10:09:32-08:00","id":1372735,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Katamari_Naneke</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1372694-mortal-martial-artists#post1372694\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do mortal martial artists play any significant role in your stories? I'm keen to have mortal dojos running around the setting. Say, that brothel is actually run by Dreaming Pearl Courtesan stylists who keep a library of secrets to build political power. This criminal gang is actually a school of corrupt Ebon Shadow Stylists that my ESS player can either defeat or take over and reform. Some wise Crane Stylists keep a tea shop and help people navigate personal crises, Black Claw stylists hang out being creepy and probably worshiping demons, and literally every other dojo is plagued by brash White Reaper Stylists challenging them to prove their worth.<br /> <br /> Different dojos of the same style could be loosely affiliated, but still distinct. Most of them could count on each other for shelter and support (White Reaper Stylists will probably fight each other, but they'll have a beer together afterwards.)<br /> <br /> The trouble I have is that there isn't a lot of mechanical difference between them. I can sort of dummy it up a bit by giving them relevant specialties (i.e. Ebon Shadow Stylists get a MA specialty in &quot;surprise attacks,&quot; White Reaper Stylists get one in &quot;while outnumbered&quot;) but I doubt player characters would even know the difference. Maybe I could make up some custom merits, or figure out some way to give them very limited access to charms? Do any of you have better ideas?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Rand's Martial Arts book and mine include optional gimmicks for MA stylists. Mine are <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/287741/Many-Limbed-Manual?src=also_purchased\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, Rand's <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/272809/The-Thousand-Sanctioned-Beasts--Martial-Artists?term=Sanctioned\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> Neither include the Core MAs, but should give some ideas. I've included mortal martial artists as mooks, gangasters, and so on. Usually as minions for an exalt or godblooded.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The Book of Laughing Serpents Series(Latest <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/293793/Book-of-Laughing-Serpents-Volume-7\" target=\"_blank\">Here</a>)<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/287741/Many-Limbed-Manual?src=hottest_filtered&amp;filters=45622\" target=\"_blank\">Many Limbed Manual</a><br /> Patreon here: <a href=\"https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety\" target=\"_blank\">https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety</a><br /> San Jeanro Co-Op writer. Volume 1 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/278871/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 2 <a href=\"https://t.co/SXRLElZlw4?amp=1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 3 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/297692/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-3?affiliate_id=389642\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> My folklore and horror blog, here:<a href=\"http://undeadauthorsociety.wordpres.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://undeadauthorsociety.com</a>","edited":{"userid":11835,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11835-epee102","user":"Epee102","date":". 03-04-2020, 01:18 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11835-epee102","name":"Epee102","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11835_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-04T11:38:30-08:00","id":1372768,"title":"","content":"Let them use weapon tags with their fists. A snake stylists penetrating fang fingers are piercing flexible attacks, a earth dragon can make smashing attacks, etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-04T21:36:34-08:00","id":1372894,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Katamari_Naneke</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1372694-mortal-martial-artists#post1372694\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do mortal martial artists play any significant role in your stories? I'm keen to have mortal dojos running around the setting. Say, that brothel is actually run by Dreaming Pearl Courtesan stylists who keep a library of secrets to build political power. This criminal gang is actually a school of corrupt Ebon Shadow Stylists that my ESS player can either defeat or take over and reform. Some wise Crane Stylists keep a tea shop and help people navigate personal crises, Black Claw stylists hang out being creepy and probably worshiping demons, and literally every other dojo is plagued by brash White Reaper Stylists challenging them to prove their worth.<br /> <br /> Different dojos of the same style could be loosely affiliated, but still distinct. Most of them could count on each other for shelter and support (White Reaper Stylists will probably fight each other, but they'll have a beer together afterwards.)<br /> <br /> The trouble I have is that there isn't a lot of mechanical difference between them. I can sort of dummy it up a bit by giving them relevant specialties (i.e. Ebon Shadow Stylists get a MA specialty in &quot;surprise attacks,&quot; White Reaper Stylists get one in &quot;while outnumbered&quot;) but I doubt player characters would even know the difference. Maybe I could make up some custom merits, or figure out some way to give them very limited access to charms? Do any of you have better ideas?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's hard for mortals to matter in 3e already because the cool stuff requires essence use, which they can't do. There rules of Exalted are really abstracted so there isn't a system to model the Southern Tiger Fist style vs the Western Iron Shirt style. That's something you'd have to do in a non-exalted system. It's almost impossible to have a Li Mu Bai fight a Pai Mei and then have that fight interrupted by Lu Bu without making them all Exalted. At best, I've used them like the Exalted equivalent of Churches and Bishops, political figures of renown, pull, and riches who's authority comes from their role at the temple. The best mortal martial artist in Creation is probably a speed bump to a combat focused DB and certainly nothing of note to even a non-com Solar/Lunar who has a basic combat investment. I doubt any mortal is capable of beating a Blood Ape in solo combat, and having one of those is pretty tame for Exalted.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Please be warned: this is not champagne, this is most likely a duck.<br /> -<i>Chausse</i><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#800080\"><i>Message me for Japanese translations.</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8830-sorcerous-overlord","name":"Sorcerous Overlord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8830_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-04T21:51:06-08:00","id":1372896,"title":"","content":"I disagree; if nothing else, certain styles will have philosophies that they follow that can be reflected. The Ebon Shadow should focus on launching an immediate Decisive from stealth to kill or poison his foe as early as possible; the Crane will fight to disable rather than to kill, and find room between her attacks for enlightening social actions; the Black Claw will want to play up his righteousness and manipulate observers to step in and help. <br /> <br /> They just won\u2019t be <i>as good at it</i> as Exalts.<br /> <br /> Not everything needs to be codified into hard widgets for characters to play differently from one another.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 03-05-2020, 08:37 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-04T22:12:27-08:00","id":1372900,"title":"","content":"Model them as a thaumaturge whose gimmick is 'always in Crane Form' or 'Fists of Searing Edge' or the neat MA Charm of your choice. No need to track the NPC's mote pool, or even have them do more than the one Charm if they're mortal.<br /> <br /> I haven't used mortal martial artists in my games. Out of 10 players across 2 games I have 0 martial artists, so the wide world of Wuxia is never the top priority. But I would use mortal martial artists if the situation called for it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/10wrFXvyXnNjaFJ0XrHdIwce6rnG__0k9/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Sidereal Jumpstart</a> (3e fanwork Charmset)<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1DQXwMXm8G1IEYLl-SmuFgKGugeZxQL63/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Cascades</a> (the above in flowchart form)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1103-tikor","name":"Tikor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1103_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"826"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-05T06:10:46-08:00","id":1372950,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1372694-mortal-martial-artists?p=1372896#post1372896\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I disagree; if nothing else, certain styles will have philosophies that they follow that can be reflected. The Ebon Shadow should focus on launching an immediate Decisive from stealth to kill or poison his foe as early as possible; the Crane will fight to disable rather than to kill, and find room between her attacks for enlightening social actions; the Black Claw will want to play up his righteousness and manipulate observers to step in and help.<br /> <br /> They just won\u2019t be <i>as good at it</i> as Exalts.<br /> <br /> Not everything needs to be codified into hard widgets for characters to play differently from one another.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> None of this is based on their actual martial arts ability, its fluffing their attacks. You could make an equal example for Archery, Melee, Brawl, or Thrown, and it wouldn't make them into several different abilities. Martial Arts in Exalted aren't judo or taekwondo, they are mystical esoteric practices that mortals cannot master. Could a Taekwondo fighter use their long kicks against a Boxers duck and weave? sure. Is that repped in the dice? no.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Please be warned: this is not champagne, this is most likely a duck.<br /> -<i>Chausse</i><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#800080\"><i>Message me for Japanese translations.</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8830-sorcerous-overlord","name":"Sorcerous Overlord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8830_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-05T07:41:08-08:00","id":1372964,"title":"","content":"Well, there is a way for Mortals to access Martial Arts Charms... Mystic Martial Arts Sorcerous Initiation, followed by the Merit: Martial Sorcery (for the respective Martial Art). We adopted this in our games This can be found in the Storytellers Vault 3rd Edition Exalted on DTRPG (<i><b>Sorcerous Ways: Mystic Martial Arts - </b>Kudos to Drew Stevens for writing it</i>). May not be completely Canon, but it is pretty awesome nonetheless. It is somewhat merit point intensive, however. Not that I worry about that all that much... this game is meant to be played on the long term. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> We have many Mortal Martial Artists in our Game currently (most of them just bog-standard Martial Artists with no supernatural access), but they are all NPC's, as we are playing Solar characters.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">The problem with defending the purity of the English language is that English is about as pure as a cribhouse whore. We don't just borrow words; on occasion, English has pursued other languages down alleyways to beat them unconscious and rifle their pockets for new vocabulary. - James. D. Nicoll</span></span></i>","edited":{"userid":540,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/540-tymeaus-jalynsfein","user":"Tymeaus Jalynsfein","date":". 03-05-2020, 11:32 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/540-tymeaus-jalynsfein","name":"Tymeaus Jalynsfein","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-05T08:27:48-08:00","id":1372975,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sorcerous Overlord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1372694-mortal-martial-artists?p=1372950#post1372950\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">None of this is based on their actual martial arts ability...</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure it is. But it's also a function of their Stealth Ability (in the case of the Ebon Shadow), Presence Ability (for the Crane), and Performance Ability (for the Black Claw). You'll note in the individual martial arts' write-ups, it lists complementary Abilities; those are there for a reason. Nor is the section describing the <i>methods</i> of the style wasted space - a mortal player can find plenty of inspiration there.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sorcerous Overlord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1372694-mortal-martial-artists?p=1372950#post1372950\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...its fluffing their attacks.</div> </div> </div> </div>The result of an Ebon Shadow putting a knife in you from stealth is quite different from a Crane disarming you and giving you stern words about the error of your ways, even if both are resolved as attacks. It's not just fluff.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sorcerous Overlord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1372694-mortal-martial-artists?p=1372950#post1372950\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You could make an equal example for Archery, Melee, Brawl, or Thrown, and it wouldn't make them into several different abilities.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thrown is not Martial Arts. But it's worth pointing out that you ignored two Abilities that <i>are</i> like Martial Arts - Craft, and Lore. Those two are both Abilities where <i>how</i> you came to have them, makes all the difference in how they can be applied.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sorcerous Overlord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1372694-mortal-martial-artists?p=1372950#post1372950\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Martial Arts in Exalted aren't judo or taekwondo, they are mystical esoteric practices that mortals cannot master.</div> </div> </div> </div>If the only practitioners of martial arts were the supernatural ones, the practice as a whole would constantly be in danger of dying out.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sorcerous Overlord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1372694-mortal-martial-artists?p=1372950#post1372950\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Could a Taekwondo fighter use their long kicks against a Boxers duck and weave? sure. Is that repped in the dice? no.</div> </div> </div> </div>But I could probably build a Taekwondo fighter and a Boxer and have them fight each other and have them <i>feel</i> pretty different; certain arts, for instance, will favor certain tactics over others, even if they can't back them up with supernatural widgets.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 03-05-2020, 11:37 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-05T08:30:25-08:00","id":1372976,"title":"","content":"Contrary to what some will tell you, there <i>is</i> a fairly functional game underneath the pile of Charms. You can, in theory, play an entire game as mortals.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-05T08:33:52-08:00","id":1372977,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1372694-mortal-martial-artists?p=1372976#post1372976\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Contrary to what some will tell you, there <i>is</i> a fairly functional game underneath the pile of Charms. You can, in theory, play an entire game as mortals.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> This is a very good point that I think a lot of people miss...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">The problem with defending the purity of the English language is that English is about as pure as a cribhouse whore. We don't just borrow words; on occasion, English has pursued other languages down alleyways to beat them unconscious and rifle their pockets for new vocabulary. - James. D. Nicoll</span></span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/540-tymeaus-jalynsfein","name":"Tymeaus Jalynsfein","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-05T12:53:55-08:00","id":1373046,"title":"","content":"So, I\u2019ve said something like this before about the Mortal Terrestrial Martial Artists of previous editions but for the most part, the charms themselves didn\u2019t really do very much.<br /> <br /> #1 Having charms to obtain shut down the part of people\u2019s brain which would in any other situation be going \u201cwhy are so many of these villagers (ability) 4? that\u2019s so unrealistic!\u201d and replaced it with \u201chey, it\u2019s wuxia! I don\u2019t have to explain shit!\u201d<br /> #2 Most TMA styles had charms which utilised underhand strategies such as ambush or poison. Using essence-based powers to do this made people more forgiving of these tactics than if say the inn keeper poisoned their character's tea.<br /> #3 Before magic became involved 2e had no time at all for characters who fought without weapons or armour. A lot of TMAs were countering weaknesses created by their own equipment restrictions.<br /> <br /> As such, I'm pretty partial to a solution like this for mortal martial artists when you don't want something like Mist the Eternal Revolutionary or Ku Nenaveya.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1372694-mortal-martial-artists?p=1372768#post1372768\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Let them use weapon tags with their fists. A snake stylists penetrating fang fingers are piercing flexible attacks, a earth dragon can make smashing attacks, etc.</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-05T20:09:33-08:00","id":1373139,"title":"","content":"John Doe - I mean, next arc or not, it is 100% the case in any game I run now. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> I had the idea when I wanted to make a Dawn-caste courtier who branched out from Dreaming Pearl Courtesan style, and I had the idea of taking a bunch of contacts in various dojos. I ended up scrapping the character concept, but I'm glad it gave me the idea of the mortal martial arts societies.<br /> <br /> I reckon DrLoveMonkey's idea about the tags is perfect. It gives some mechanical specialisation without bogging things down with bookkeeping for fairly minor combatants. I can also describe it easily in fights between mortals that the PCs don't deign to engage with.<br /> <br /> Lioness, you got me, I am guilty of this. Alucard has a bunch of good points about different tactics and different goals in a fight, too.<br /> <br /> Thanks everyone, this is a lot to work with!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24421-katamari_naneke","name":"Katamari_Naneke","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"83"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-05T22:16:59-08:00","id":1373154,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1372694-mortal-martial-artists?p=1372975#post1372975\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The result of an Ebon Shadow putting a knife in you from stealth is quite different from a Crane disarming you and giving you stern words about the error of your ways, even if both are resolved as attacks. It's not just fluff.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's no mechanical incentive for either of these abilities, and there's nothing stopping an Ebon Shadower from disarming you and giving you a stern talking to. Yes, you absolutely can have them act in different ways, but that's making a personal choice about how they act, it's not different martial art. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Thrown is not Martial Arts. </div> </div> </div>I'm really curious bout why you skipped Melee, Archery, and Brawl only to state the absolute obvious. I'm not really sure what you mean here. But going back to your example about Crane and ES, a Greek Hoplite throwing a spear from the shield wall is different from the Ninja throwing a kunai and Viking tossing a hatchet, but no one is suggestion that really there's 3 different kinds of Thrown, even though mechanically there's only one. Are those different characters, philosophies, and styles? absolutely. Does it matter in game? not really. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> But it's worth pointing out that you ignored two Abilities that <i>are</i> like Martial Arts - Craft, and Lore. Those two are both Abilities where <i>how</i> you came to have them, makes all the difference in how they can be applied. </div> </div> </div>Uhh, I guess? I don't really understand what you mean here. I think you mean something like Craft: Swords and Craft: Ships are two different things? I'm not sure &quot;how you came to have them&quot; has any effect in game. Is there a difference between a DaVinci type swordsmith who is a self-taught genius vs a protege of Alveua, who is also a swordsmith? they both hammer out swords. <br /> <br /> I don't understand the Lore thing at all. Unless you mean something like Lore: Blessed Isle and Lore: Military. Even then, it doesn't match Martial Arts because there's only one set of Lore charms with a restriction on how you use them, which is the polar opposite of 10+ MAs with mechanical incentives to use different combat philosophies. <br /> <br /> I don't get where this comparison was supposed to go. Moving on:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If the only practitioners of martial arts were the supernatural ones, the practice as a whole would constantly be in danger of dying out. </div> </div> </div>I mean, lost techniques from a bygone age of heroes that have to be rediscovered in the present is a staple of Wuxia. In Universe, Tiger Style and Ebon Shadow are Supernatural. They aren't just another type of kickboxing. Mortals, with perhaps a handful of rare exceptions, literally cannot do them. There could be 100 dojos teaching mundane Tiger Style and offshoots waiting for a prodigy to come and unlock the supernatural side of them (another common Wuxia trope), but there's no reason they would be dying out. <br /> <br /> [/QUOTE]But I could probably build a Taekwondo fighter and a Boxer and have them fight each other and have them <i>feel</i> pretty different; certain arts, for instance, will favor certain tactics over others, even if they can't back them up with supernatural widgets.[/QUOTE]<br /> As discussed early, I don't think so on a meaningful level. The boxer boxes, the Tae Kwon Doer kicks. Maybe one takes a full defense, or a rush, or a whatever, but there's really not much for them to do in Exalted beyond roll with a specialty and stunt. There's no mechanic for the boxer to close inside of kicking range staying low and pummeling the gut of the kicker, just as there's no mechanic that gives the kicker advantage for footsies and zoning out the boxer when they try to close distance. That's a step toward granularity, while Exalted takes a step (actually a couple of steps) toward abstraction. <br /> <br /> There are many posts in this thread about how you could make them <i>feel</i> different by doing XYZ, but I'm looking at this a level removed: there isn't a difference with the math, the dice, the options, or anything else mechanical/out of game. Just like there's only one skill for Melee but hundreds of types of fighters (Viking, Samurai, Jaguar Warrior, Centurion, Landsknecht...), non-charm using Martial Artists all work the same way.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Please be warned: this is not champagne, this is most likely a duck.<br /> -<i>Chausse</i><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#800080\"><i>Message me for Japanese translations.</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8830-sorcerous-overlord","name":"Sorcerous Overlord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8830_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-05T23:48:11-08:00","id":1373157,"title":"","content":"Gonna go ahead and spoiler my reply to <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8830-sorcerous-overlord\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar8830_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"8830\" data-vbnamecard=\"8830\">Sorcerous Overlord</a> , though I <i>hope</i> I'm not boring the rest of y'all to tears... <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sorcerous Overlord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1372694-mortal-martial-artists?p=1373154#post1373154\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's no mechanical incentive for either of these abilities\u2026</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure there is. Unexpected attacks penalize the enemy\u2019s defense by 2; likewise, a successful Disarm prevents the defender from being able to attack with their weapon, absent some means to retrieve it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sorcerous Overlord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1372694-mortal-martial-artists?p=1373154#post1373154\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u2026and there's nothing stopping an Ebon Shadower from disarming you and giving you a stern talking to.</div> </div> </div> </div>His lack of Presence dots might make his argument less compelling.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sorcerous Overlord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1372694-mortal-martial-artists?p=1373154#post1373154\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, you absolutely can have them act in different ways, but that's making a personal choice about how they act, it's not different martial art.</div> </div> </div> </div>I disagree; we have different Martial Arts <i>because</i> each is intended to have a central theme that it follows, even before Charms.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sorcerous Overlord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1372694-mortal-martial-artists?p=1373154#post1373154\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm really curious bout why you skipped Melee, Archery, and Brawl only to state the absolute obvious.</div> </div> </div> </div>Mostly because if I included the whole list, it would add to what was already a lengthy post.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sorcerous Overlord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1372694-mortal-martial-artists?p=1373154#post1373154\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But going back to your example about Crane and ES, a Greek Hoplite throwing a spear from the shield wall is different from the Ninja throwing a kunai and Viking tossing a hatchet, but <b>no one is suggestion[sic]</b> that really there's 3 different kinds of Thrown, even though mechanically there's only one.</div> </div> </div> </div><i>I\u2019d</i> suggest it. I argued for it years back. A lack of discrete widgets should not render your Ability dots flavorless. If your character learned Medicine dots from Skullstone's necrosurgery college, it should be a different experience than learning them via the drug operations in Great Forks. You should be excellent at amputating limbs, versus being amazing at treating addiction.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sorcerous Overlord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1372694-mortal-martial-artists?p=1373154#post1373154\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are those different characters, philosophies, and styles? absolutely. <b>Does it matter in game? not really.</b></div> </div> </div> </div>Again, I disagree.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sorcerous Overlord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1372694-mortal-martial-artists?p=1373154#post1373154\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think you mean something like Craft: Swords and Craft: Ships are two different things?</div> </div> </div> </div>That\u2019s part of it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sorcerous Overlord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1372694-mortal-martial-artists?p=1373154#post1373154\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not sure &quot;how you came to have them&quot; has any effect in game.</div> </div> </div> </div>There\u2019s <i>a bevy</i> of Merits you can take for sorcery, defined by \u201chow you came to have them.\u201d None learns The Burning Name studying under Mara.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sorcerous Overlord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1372694-mortal-martial-artists?p=1373154#post1373154\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is there a difference between a DaVinci type swordsmith who is a self-taught genius vs a protege of Alveua, who is also a swordsmith? they both hammer out swords.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Da Vinci type doesn\u2019t hammer his swords out of <i>people</i>.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sorcerous Overlord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1372694-mortal-martial-artists?p=1373154#post1373154\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Even then, it doesn't match Martial Arts because there's only one set of Lore charms with a restriction on how you use them, which is the polar opposite of 10+ MAs with mechanical incentives to use different combat philosophies.</div> </div> </div> </div>It\u2019s still a closer match than Melee.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sorcerous Overlord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1372694-mortal-martial-artists?p=1373154#post1373154\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In Universe, Tiger Style and Ebon Shadow are Supernatural. They aren't just another type of kickboxing.</div> </div> </div> </div>You say that like it can\u2019t be both.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sorcerous Overlord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1372694-mortal-martial-artists?p=1373154#post1373154\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mortals, with perhaps a handful of rare exceptions, literally cannot do them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Lacking the enlightenment to draw out magical techniques from understanding of the mortal skill, is not lacking the capacity to understand the mortal skill.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sorcerous Overlord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1372694-mortal-martial-artists?p=1373154#post1373154\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As discussed early, I don't think so on a meaningful level. The boxer boxes, the Tae Kwon Doer kicks. Maybe one takes a full defense, or a rush, or a whatever, but there's really not much for them to do in Exalted beyond roll with a specialty and stunt.</div> </div> </div> </div>Consider looking past dice, at the underlying philosophies.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sorcerous Overlord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1372694-mortal-martial-artists?p=1373154#post1373154\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's no mechanic for the boxer to close inside of kicking range staying low and pummeling the gut of the kicker, just as there's no mechanic that gives the kicker advantage for footsies and zoning out the boxer when they try to close distance.</div> </div> </div> </div>It\u2019s below the <i>typical</i> level of system resolution; that doesn\u2019t mean it <i>must</i> be ignored. An ST is encouraged to award or penalize where necessary, after all; and if I was running a mortal game, that\u2019s <i>exactly </i>what I\u2019d be doing for the boxer who can\u2019t escape the kicker (and for the kicker when the boxer has outwaited his opponent\u2019s stamina and starts his own flurry of blows).<br /> <br /> I actually did that when I was running Exalts; Seamstress, a necrosurgeon, had a comatose patient. Pitiless Triage Judgment informed her that a blow to the head had cracked his skull, and that the inflammation in his brain (and a piece of skull not being where it should!) was what was keeping him under. When she was asked to suggest a medicine to reduce the swelling in his brain, I assigned her a dice penalty to the roll; as someone who learned her trade cutting on corpses, this was outside her wheelhouse.<br /> <br /> (He recovered, by the way. There was a Guild factor handy with a whole wagon full of drugs.)</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 03-06-2020, 12:06 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-06T05:22:21-08:00","id":1373177,"title":"","content":"If people are looking for mechanical differences, might I suggest specialties?<br /> <br /> Or just... you know, the Ebon Shadow martial artists have dots of Stealth, the White Veil users have Socialise, the Earth Dragon users have Resistance, etc.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-06T05:47:13-08:00","id":1373183,"title":"","content":"I actually planned to use mortal martial artists a fair bit in my current game, but none of the PCs were martial artists and there was a lot of other stuff going on, so I didn't really bother in the end.<br /> <br /> The ST of one of the games I play likes to use them though. Martial Arts organisations, duels, philosophical debates between sifus, and so on. Sure, I guess there's not a ton of mechanical difference between the mortal ones... but we're Essence 4 Solars, does it really matter?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-06T06:14:06-08:00","id":1373185,"title":"","content":"A Melee knife-fighter has the same accuracy, damage and Parry as an unarmed Brawler (after stunting).<br /> <br /> Straight swords and slashing swords have the same stats.<br /> <br /> Heck, if you pick up the broken leg of a barstool during a bar-room brawl the your damage, accuracy and Parry doesn't change from simply being unarmed because clubs have the same stats as fists.<br /> <br /> Exalted isn't really about having that high a level of system granularity.<br /> <br /> I don't think complaining that Ebon Shadow and Crane styles are too similar is a valid complaint if they're also identical to Brawl and Melee.<br /> <br /> I mean, I get <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8830-sorcerous-overlord\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar8830_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"8830\" data-vbnamecard=\"8830\">Sorcerous Overlord</a> wants a higher level of granularity across the board, but I don't see an advantage to doing it that way. In D&amp;D you roll your D20, add your modifiers and compare to AC. I don't want to go back to pages of THAC0 style charts to cross reference what body part I hit when using a round-house kick against a boxer.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-06T06:52:59-08:00","id":1373189,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1372694-mortal-martial-artists?p=1373183#post1373183\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">but we're Essence 4 Solars, does it really matter?</div> </div> </div> </div>You're not the first to raise this point, and it's a fair one. It'd take a whole lot of them to make it worth pulling out the dice rather than just narrating the results. Which makes me wonder, does anyone have ideas for representing a mass combat unit of mortal martial artists? I think it's likely to come up at some point as a group of antagonists, and it's certain to come up when my Ebon Shadow Stylist player manages to train his army of ninjas.<br /> <br /> Speaking of which, I'm thinking of putting together a custom charm enhancing Tiger Warrior Training Technique to help him do that. Something that allows elite martial artists to be trained, and probably offers some training in complementary abilities. It might be cool to come up with an extra add-on for each style (comparable to Demon-Fighting Principle, Giant-Slaying Tactics etc) that gives some unique benefit, but there are so many styles. Still, maybe I can just come up with ideas that that character might use and then crowdsource the rest. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24421-katamari_naneke","name":"Katamari_Naneke","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"83"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-06T07:02:40-08:00","id":1373193,"title":"","content":"Hmmm, the Tiger-Warrior extra ability training is a good idea.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-06T07:03:14-08:00","id":1373194,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Katamari_Naneke</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1372694-mortal-martial-artists?p=1373189#post1373189\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You're not the first to raise this point, and it's a fair one. It'd take a whole lot of them to make it worth pulling out the dice rather than just narrating the results. Which makes me wonder, does anyone have ideas for representing a mass combat unit of mortal martial artists? I think it's likely to come up at some point as a group of antagonists, and it's certain to come up when my Ebon Shadow Stylist player manages to train his army of ninjas.<br /> <br /> Speaking of which, I'm thinking of putting together a custom charm enhancing Tiger Warrior Training Technique to help him do that. Something that allows elite martial artists to be trained, and probably offers some training in complementary abilities. It might be cool to come up with an extra add-on for each style (comparable to Demon-Fighting Principle, Giant-Slaying Tactics etc) that gives some unique benefit, but there are so many styles. Still, maybe I can just come up with ideas that that character might use and then crowdsource the rest. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I swaer someone has done that charm...but I can't find it on the Wiki. Hm.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The Book of Laughing Serpents Series(Latest <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/293793/Book-of-Laughing-Serpents-Volume-7\" target=\"_blank\">Here</a>)<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/287741/Many-Limbed-Manual?src=hottest_filtered&amp;filters=45622\" target=\"_blank\">Many Limbed Manual</a><br /> Patreon here: <a href=\"https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety\" target=\"_blank\">https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety</a><br /> San Jeanro Co-Op writer. Volume 1 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/278871/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 2 <a href=\"https://t.co/SXRLElZlw4?amp=1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 3 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/297692/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-3?affiliate_id=389642\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> My folklore and horror blog, here:<a href=\"http://undeadauthorsociety.wordpres.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://undeadauthorsociety.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11835-epee102","name":"Epee102","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11835_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-06T09:11:58-08:00","id":1373214,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1372694-mortal-martial-artists?p=1373046#post1373046\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As such, I'm pretty partial to a solution like this for mortal martial artists when you don't want something like Mist the Eternal Revolutionary or Ku Nenaveya.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh right, if you go here I strongly suggest any NPC you give a mote pool to has a way of spending more than 5m/round.<br /> <br /> In 2.0 when &quot;enlightened mortal&quot; became a distinct thing motes were only rewarded when you made a stunt and suceeded on the action. This meant that a charm that cost 1m for the potential to knock someone prone was worth tracking because if the martial artist kept attacking and missing they'd exhaust themselves but in 3rd edtion mote recovery is fixed so they can spend that kind of essence every round until the sun explodes and an initiative cost is now a much better way to realise that goal on a character who wouldn't have a lot of things to spend their essence on hence tags like Smashing, Piercing and Chopping. The canonical antagonists don't always achieve this but the better ones do.<br /> <br /> Lastly, don't feel you have to avoid dice adders (including sucess increasing, target number reducer, re-rolls etc) because of old 2e sensibilities.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-06T20:03:12-08:00","id":1373314,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1372694-mortal-martial-artists?p=1373157#post1373157\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sure there is. Unexpected attacks penalize the enemy\u2019s defense by 2; likewise, a successful Disarm prevents the defender from being able to attack with their weapon, absent some means to retrieve it.</div> </div> </div> </div>So right off the bat, here's a misunderstanding- I'm not saying there isn't a mechanical incentive to making Ambush or Disarm Gambits, I'm saying there's no extra bonus for a doing an ambush as an Ebon Shadower (-ist?) without charms. Yes, Ebon Shadow compliments stealth. Yes, that's what I would expect and Ebon Shade to do. But Ambush from Stealth 3 ES 3 and no charms is <i>the exact same </i>as Ambush from Stealth 3 Crane 3 with no charms. That's it. there's no passive bonus just from ES itself. That's what the form Charm is for.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> His lack of Presence dots might make his argument less compelling. </div> </div> </div>Again, the issue here is there's no non-charm synergy between Crane and Presence beyond 'I want to RP the strict kung fu master'. You can RP the strict Ninja master the same way using ES. There's literally 0 difference as a mechanic.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>None (sic) learns The Burning Name studying under Mara</b> </div> </div> </div>There's really nothing stopping you. You could have used your sex kung fu to steal it from an elemental lover under her tutelage.<br /> <br /> I'm not gonna go through the rest because it's just us going around in circles about this point. I think we've both made our case.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar531_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"531\" data-vbnamecard=\"531\">JohnDoe244</a> I don't <i>want</i> a higher level of granularity, I'm just pointing out that Exalted doesn't do it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Please be warned: this is not champagne, this is most likely a duck.<br /> -<i>Chausse</i><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#800080\"><i>Message me for Japanese translations.</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8830-sorcerous-overlord","name":"Sorcerous Overlord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8830_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-06T21:46:50-08:00","id":1373324,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sorcerous Overlord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1372694-mortal-martial-artists?p=1373314#post1373314\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, Ebon Shadow compliments stealth. Yes, that's what I would expect and [sic] Ebon Shade to do. But Ambush from Stealth 3 ES 3 and no charms is <i>the exact same </i>as Ambush from Stealth 3 Crane 3 with no charms.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure, in which case, the question arises, why is the Crane built like an Ebon Shadow guy and not like a Crane?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sorcerous Overlord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1372694-mortal-martial-artists?p=1373314#post1373314\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's really nothing stopping you.</div> </div> </div> </div>What about the desire for the appearance of a coherent character?<br /> <br /> (Also, I\u2019d probably not allow \u201cI seduced an elemental\u201d to justify The Burning Name at my table.)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sorcerous Overlord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1372694-mortal-martial-artists?p=1373314#post1373314\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I think we've both made our case.</div> </div> </div> </div>Fair enough.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 03-07-2020, 12:50 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-08T13:10:11-07:00","id":1373596,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Katamari_Naneke</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1372694-mortal-martial-artists#post1372694\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do mortal martial artists play any significant role in your stories? I'm keen to have mortal dojos running around the setting. Say, that brothel is actually run by Dreaming Pearl Courtesan stylists who keep a library of secrets to build political power. This criminal gang is actually a school of corrupt Ebon Shadow Stylists that my ESS player can either defeat or take over and reform. Some wise Crane Stylists keep a tea shop and help people navigate personal crises, Black Claw stylists hang out being creepy and probably worshiping demons, and literally every other dojo is plagued by brash White Reaper Stylists challenging them to prove their worth.<br /> <br /> Different dojos of the same style could be loosely affiliated, but still distinct. Most of them could count on each other for shelter and support (White Reaper Stylists will probably fight each other, but they'll have a beer together afterwards.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Late to this, apologies, but if you've not seen it already you may wanna check out <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/238143/Adversaries-of-the-Righteous-Ashana-Ikatu\" target=\"_blank\">Adversaries of the Righteous: Ashana Ikatu</a>.<br /> <br /> Her whole schtick is heading up a dojo, plus she has a special power that buffs snake style users who have a positive tie to her (e.g. students) \u2013 v. 'enlightened mortal martial artist Ex3e vintage' vibes.<br /> <br /> Might offer some idea fodder...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24647,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24647-moss-reynholm","user":"Moss Reynholm","date":". 03-08-2020, 04:14 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24647-moss-reynholm","name":"Moss Reynholm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24647_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-09T02:13:04-07:00","id":1373705,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Katamari_Naneke</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1372694-mortal-martial-artists#post1372694\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do mortal martial artists play any significant role in your stories? <br /> The trouble I have is that there isn't a lot of mechanical difference between them. I can sort of dummy it up a bit by giving them relevant specialties (i.e. Ebon Shadow Stylists get a MA specialty in &quot;surprise attacks,&quot; White Reaper Stylists get one in &quot;while outnumbered&quot;) but I doubt player characters would even know the difference. Maybe I could make up some custom merits, or figure out some way to give them very limited access to charms? Do any of you have better ideas?</div> </div> </div> </div>In Second Edition Martial Artists and Martial Art schools played a really big role in my games due to the way that Awakened Mortal Martial Artists were sort of a head above normal mortal warriors. My players tended to spend a lot of time figuring out ways to get their mortal followers trained (either as Martial Artists, Sorcerers or Thaumatuges), coming up with martial art styles and Charms for them and whatnot.<br /> <br /> I've noticed in Third Edition, without the mechanical distinction, my players don't really care all that much and will o just have their mortal followers default to generic Melee or Archery or whatever rather than Martial Arts. Even the one player who specifically wanted a group of Ninja dudes as followers still build them with melee and thrown rather than Martial Arts. Players still take Martial Arts for themselves, but as something they would focus on for NPC followers and whatnot, it's kind of vanished. <br /> <br /> From the GM side, when Martial Art schools or organizations pop up, they tend to fill the same role as any other local political faction (like a religious order, or the local thieves guild, merchant guild or what have you). Overall, Martial Arts as a whole definitely doesn't play as large of a role in my games these days as they used to.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-09T05:31:54-07:00","id":1373742,"title":"","content":"Thanks for the tip, Moss! And it's only too late if people start accusing you of thread necromancy. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> I think that's a shame, Anubis, but maybe you've already exhausted this idea's potential for interesting stories. I just really like the idea of Martial Arts as institutions as well as individuals' philosophies &amp; combat tactics.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24421-katamari_naneke","name":"Katamari_Naneke","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"83"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}